    "text": "For any <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></math> matrix <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>, let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>|</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>|</mo></math> denote the determinant of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math> be the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></math> identity matrix. Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math>&nbsp;be two <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></math> matrices such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>E</mi><mi>F</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is invertible. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>E</mi><mi>F</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, then which of the following statements is (are) TRUE ?",
